  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37131398",
      "title": "Mutating Values in Memory",
      "lectureOrder": 73,
      "videoOrder": 67,
      "sourceHash": "66bcf62de6a33ca4d46287dc86f8535ae02340aa540fe3c8603c1dffd39f50a8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.82,
          "en": "So how can we shuffle these list items here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.82,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "Well, that thankfully is easy enough to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "because Flutter gives you a shuffle method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 14.673,
          "en": "that can be called on lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.87,
          "end": 18.27,
          "en": "So just as map could be called on lists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.27,
          "end": 20.49,
          "en": "shuffle can also be called on lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.49,
          "end": 23.34,
          "en": "It's a built-in method that can be called on lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.34,
          "end": 27.06,
          "en": "to change the order of the items in the list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.06,
          "end": 30.78,
          "en": "However, what's important to understand regarding shuffle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.78,
          "end": 35.78,
          "en": "is that unlike map, it does change the original list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.09,
          "end": 38.94,
          "en": "Map does not change the original list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 40.86,
          "en": "Shuffle does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.86,
          "end": 44.67,
          "en": "And I actually don't wanna change this list of answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.67,
          "end": 47.22,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that the correct answer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.22,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "stays the first answer here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 52.59,
          "en": "and therefore we have to first copy this list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.59,
          "end": 54.42,
          "en": "before we shuffle it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.42,
          "end": 57.81,
          "en": "Otherwise, finding out which answer was the correct answer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.81,
          "end": 61.92,
          "en": "will impossible after these answers have been shuffled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 63.45,
          "en": "So therefore, here, to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.45,
          "end": 66.48,
          "en": "that we're shuffling the answers in a brand new list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.48,
          "end": 68.82,
          "en": "we can go to this QuizQuestion class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.82,
          "end": 70.26,
          "en": "which we added earlier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.26,
          "end": 73.77,
          "en": "which is our blueprint for these questions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.77,
          "end": 77.4,
          "en": "And in there we can add a function, a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.4,
          "end": 82.4,
          "en": "that could be called getShuffledAnswers like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 86.07,
          "en": "This should return a list of string values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.07,
          "end": 89.253,
          "en": "so the same data type as we used it here for answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 92.91,
          "en": "And inside of getShuffledAnswers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 95.97,
          "en": "I therefore what I call this shuffle method on answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.97,
          "end": 100.32,
          "en": "But I first want to create a copy of answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.32,
          "end": 104.64,
          "en": "And creating such a copy is thankfully straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.64,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "We can use the built-in List class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 112.91,
          "en": "so List is not just a type but also a class built into Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.19,
          "end": 117.66,
          "en": "And this offers a couple of utility constructor functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.66,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "that make it easy to create different lists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 124.113,
          "en": "For example, it has a of constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 129.06,
          "en": "and this of constructor function creates a new list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.06,
          "end": 131.04,
          "en": "based on another list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.04,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "So it copies an existing list basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 137.94,
          "en": "And therefore here we can pass answers to List.of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.94,
          "end": 141.393,
          "en": "to create a new list based on that old list of answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.25,
          "end": 147.03300000000002,
          "en": "And then we can call shuffle on this new list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.05,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "So now the new list will be the shuffled one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 152.55,
          "en": "and the old list will be untouched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.55,
          "end": 156.48,
          "en": "because we copied the list and then shuffle the copied list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.48,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "And what we're doing here, by the way, is called chaining.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 162.12,
          "en": "We're calling a method on the result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.12,
          "end": 164.82,
          "en": "of calling another function or method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.82,
          "end": 166.68,
          "en": "And this is something you'll see quite a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.68,
          "end": 168.75,
          "en": "when working with Dart and Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.75,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "It is quite common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 173.85,
          "en": "to chain command after command after command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.85,
          "end": 175.38,
          "en": "Now here it's of course not enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.38,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "to just shuffle the list though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 180.09,
          "en": "instead we also must return it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.09,
          "end": 184.62,
          "en": "And here it turns out that shuffle indeed returns nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 187.74,
          "en": "So shuffle does not yield the shuffled list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.74,
          "end": 191.85,
          "en": "Instead it shuffles the list on which you call it in place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.85,
          "end": 194.193,
          "en": "and does not give you the updated list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.15,
          "end": 198.78,
          "en": "Therefore, here, to get hold of that updated list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.78,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "we actually have to change the code a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 204.81,
          "en": "and first create a new final variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.81,
          "end": 207.66,
          "en": "which could be called shuffledList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.66,
          "end": 210.273,
          "en": "which is initially just the copy of the list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.32,
          "end": 216.15,
          "en": "but then we call shuffle on that shuffledList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.15,
          "end": 220.083,
          "en": "And then it's this shuffledList here, which is returned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 222.3,
          "end": 223.74,
          "en": "And we must do it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.74,
          "end": 225.93,
          "en": "so that we first create this copy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.93,
          "end": 228.84,
          "en": "and store this copy in a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "and then we call shuffle, which as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 233.7,
          "en": "changes that list in place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.7,
          "end": 237.57,
          "en": "So after this line of code, shuffledList will have changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 241.32,
          "en": "and then we return the updated shuffledList.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.32,
          "end": 243.36,
          "en": "And you might wonder how a shuffledList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.36,
          "end": 245.61,
          "en": "can change if it's final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.61,
          "end": 250.41,
          "en": "but final only ensures that you can't reassign the variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.41,
          "end": 251.85,
          "en": "So I can't, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.85,
          "end": 256.02,
          "en": "assign shuffledList to a new list here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.02,
          "end": 258.723,
          "en": "This does not work because of final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 260.824,
          "end": 262.62,
          "en": "but that's not what we're doing when calling shuffle here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.62,
          "end": 264.21,
          "en": "Instead, this reaches out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.21,
          "end": 266.79,
          "en": "to the existing list object in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.79,
          "end": 269.46,
          "en": "and edits the items in that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.46,
          "end": 272.82,
          "en": "It does not override the list as a whole.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.82,
          "end": 275.73,
          "en": "So calling shuffle here does not violate final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 275.73,
          "end": 279.544,
          "en": "because we're not reassigning a value to shuffledList,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.544,
          "end": 283.6,
          "en": "we're just editing an existing value in memory with shuffle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.46,
          "end": 285.293,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.293,
          "end": 288.96,
          "en": "we now got our getShuffledAnswers method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.96,
          "end": 291.36,
          "en": "and back in questions_screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.36,
          "end": 294.45,
          "en": "we can now use these shuffled answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.45,
          "end": 295.95,
          "en": "We can use them down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 295.95,
          "end": 299.13,
          "en": "Instead of accessing currentQuestion.answers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.13,
          "end": 303.54,
          "en": "we can access currentQuestion.getShuffledAnswers(),",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 303.54,
          "end": 308.22,
          "en": "and then map those shuffled answers to our answer buttons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 308.22,
          "end": 310.59,
          "en": "So this logic doesn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.59,
          "end": 313.95,
          "en": "We still chain this map method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.95,
          "end": 317.46,
          "en": "onto the getShuffledAnswers method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 321.69,
          "en": "but the difference now is that we map our shuffled answers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321.69,
          "end": 325.23,
          "en": "and very important we do all these things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 325.23,
          "end": 328.383,
          "en": "without changing the original answers list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 329.25,
          "end": 332.31,
          "en": "With that, you'll see that now I have a different order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 332.31,
          "end": 333.63,
          "en": "than I did before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.63,
          "end": 335.94,
          "en": "Before, Widgets was at the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.94,
          "end": 337.86,
          "en": "because this is the right answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 337.86,
          "end": 339.96,
          "en": "Now here, for me, its Functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 339.96,
          "end": 342.42,
          "en": "and the next time I'll visit this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 342.42,
